From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn-patches <tyn-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:50:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: debug mode only from the user setting

The porting tools (the status line at the top left, speed, skip, rewind,
debug-cmd.txt) were on whenever the profile has the DebugMenu game feature,
which several upstream profiles set (cclcc, chlcc, mo6tw-pc, mo6tw ...): on
those games the status line showed with the debug mode turned off in the
app. Only CommonSettings.DebugMode turns them on now; the DebugMenu feature
keeps the upstream debug menu as before.

Generic (fixes patch 0053).
Verified on MuMu (Android 15 x86_64 emulator, not a real device), sg0-pc:
DebugMode false in userconfig.toml, no status line; true, the status line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/debugtools.cpp b/src/debugtools.cpp
index dab6cde709be2179328767d1fa1a7d575c5b288c..ace5eecae220f37a5e59c5903999b66e812848d0 100644
--- a/src/debugtools.cpp
+++ b/src/debugtools.cpp
@@ -334,7 +334,7 @@ void UnlockAll() {
 }  // namespace
 
 bool Enabled() {
-  return UserConfig::CommonSettings.DebugMode || (+Profile::Game::GameFeatures & +GameFeature::DebugMenu);
+  return UserConfig::CommonSettings.DebugMode;
 }
 
 bool OpenRequested() {
diff --git a/src/debugtools.h b/src/debugtools.h
index 07bd389c0c1e516dbfa28802adcf5425f1c7c9e7..4d54ed1cba44c0fc2dab992ac3afe41f3a07a3de 100644
--- a/src/debugtools.h
+++ b/src/debugtools.h
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #pragma once
 
-// Porting tools of the debug mode (UserConfig CommonSettings.DebugMode, or the DebugMenu game feature): game speed,
+// Porting tools of the debug mode (UserConfig CommonSettings.DebugMode only; the DebugMenu game feature of some
+// upstream profiles keeps just the upstream debug menu): game speed,
 // pause and single steps, automatic snapshots for rewinding, saved states, jumps of a script thread to any label of
 // any script, skip of everything, unlocks. Shown as the "Porting" tab of the debug menu; on touch screens three
 // fingers at once open the menu.
